<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">József Antall</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1932–1993</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">József Antall was a Hungarian historian and politician who became the first freely elected prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> after communism, in 1990. As leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungarian-democratic-forum">Hungarian Democratic Forum</a> he headed a centre-right coalition that began the transition to a market economy and western integration. He died in office in December 1993.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jozsef-antall.jpg" alt="József Antall" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antall-család archívum [Antall family's archives] (Péter Antall) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:J%C3%B3zsef_Antall_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
